  "notes": "MasAir (Mas Air Cargo, Mexico) flies A330-200 and A330-300 freighters, several registered in Ireland (EI-) and some flown for it by Galistair Malta. The patchwork is far too fine to draw (hundreds of small check, stripe, dot and cube tiles): drawn as a simplified patchwork of our own (revised 2026-11-20 at the owner's review): a mid-green ground with big rhombus and parallelogram facets in dark teal, lime and a pale green-white (the fine stripes and checks averaged), sized like the photo's facets (about a third of the fuselage's height, a quarter of the fin's chord), and thirteen small hexagonal cubes in staggered columns over x 0.70-0.77 ahead of it, light green (two lime), thinning forward. The facets' places follow the photos' layout loosely, not cell by cell; the real front edge is ragged. Measured on EI-MYY (2022-06-25): 'mas' runs x 0.152-0.294 with a 2.6 m x-height; the patchwork's dense front edge stands nearly upright at x 0.77 (just ahead of the fin's root), the scattered cubes reach forward to x 0.69. EI-MAA at LAX (2026-02-11) shows the same scheme. The right side's title isn't seen in any photo (the one right-side photo, EI-MAE in 2023, has no title at all): drawn as on the left, reading normally from that side. EI-MAE flew without titles in 2022-2023; whether it still does isn't known. The A330-200s' windows are plugged (EI-MYY), but EI-MAA (2026) still shows window frames: drawn hidden. Engines carry four facets on a mid-green cowling; the winglets a dark band on green. Area count: 20 fuselage (13 small cubes, the ground, 6 facets), 9 fin, 4 engine, 1 winglet: 34. The title's face measured 2026-11-20 on the photo fit: its a has two stories (Futura's has one), and Montserrat Bold follows the letters closest, so it comes first.",
  "history": "New in the LAX round 2 (2026-11-20); MAA had no scheme here before."
